<!-- 8. RELIABILITY METRICS -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section class="py-20 md:py-28 bg-graphite" aria-labelledby="metrics-heading">
  <div class="container-x">
    <SectionHeading
      id="metrics-heading"
      index="08"
      label="Reliability Metrics"
      title="Measure what matters. Improve what you measure."
      lede="SRE is a data-driven discipline. These are the metrics we use to define, measure, and improve reliability across your systems. Each metric is chosen for its direct relationship to user experience and business outcomes."
      tone="graphite"
    />

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Service Level Indicators</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Quantitative measures of service performance. The metrics that directly reflect user experience: request latency, error rate, throughput, availability, and durability. Every SLI is carefully chosen and precisely measured.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Service Level Objectives</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Target values for each SLI that define acceptable service performance. SLOs create a shared understanding of what reliable means for each service. They are the basis for error budgets and reliability decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Service Level Agreements</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Contractual commitments to customers, typically stricter than internal SLOs. SLAs define penalties for non-compliance. We help you set achievable SLAs backed by SLOs that give early warning of breach risk.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Error Budgets</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The acceptable amount of unreliability over a time window (1 - SLO). Error budgets create a data-driven mechanism for balancing feature velocity with reliability. When the budget is available, ship features. When it is depleted, stop shipping and invest in stability.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">MTTR</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Mean Time To Recover. The average time from incident detection to full recovery. Lower MTTR means faster recovery, reduced customer impact, and less engineering time spent on incidents.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">MTTD</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Mean Time To Detect. The average time between when a failure occurs and when it is detected. Lower MTTD means faster awareness and reduced blast radius. Improved by better monitoring, alerting, and synthetic checks.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">MTBF</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">Mean Time Between Failures. The average time between consecutive system failures. Higher MTBF indicates more reliable systems. Improved through better architecture, testing, and change management.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Availability</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The proportion of time a service is operational and accessible. Measured as uptime divided by total time. Target availability depends on business requirements, not theoretical maximums.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Latency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The time taken to process a request. Measured at various percentiles: p50, p95, p99. Latency directly impacts user experience and conversion rates. Consistent low latency is a primary SLO for most services.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Throughput</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The number of requests a system can process per unit time. Measured as requests per second, transactions per second, or messages processed. Throughput capacity determines scaling requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Saturation</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The degree to which a resource is utilized. CPU, memory, disk I/O, network bandwidth, and connection pool usage. Saturation is an early indicator of capacity constraints before they impact users.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Error Rate</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The proportion of requests that result in errors. HTTP 5xx, application exceptions, and business logic failures. Error rate spikes are a primary indicator of system degradation or bugs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Deployment Frequency</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">How often your organization deploys code to production. Higher deployment frequency correlates with higher engineering velocity and organizational performance. Enabled by automation and reliable release processes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-graphite-line bg-graphite-2 p-6" data-reveal>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-graphite-fg mb-2">Change Failure Rate</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-graphite-fg-2">The percentage of deployments that result in degraded service or require remediation. Lower change failure rate indicates safer release processes. Tracked alongside deployment frequency for a complete reliability picture.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

